## Native functions whose signature a P/Invoke cannot pass yet
## (ImplementationPlan.md 5.10.13, 5.10.14; M15.b item 3; recon p2
## native-imports 6). Phase 1 marshals int32, native int, float32 and
## float64 values and void results; a natively bound function that takes or
## returns anything else (a two-value aggregate, an i128, a byval aggregate,
## an sret result, a vector, half) is the backend's error
##   native function '<name>' (<module>) takes or returns a value that a
##   P/Invoke cannot pass natively yet (phase 3)
## once per function, whether code calls it or an initializer takes its
## address, with the module it bound to. The function of the same library
## with a plain signature gets its P/Invoke as usual (its text is not
## written, since the link fails, so only the errors are checked).
## Native long double functions get the same text (the section 12 row of
## 2026-10-22 for 5.10.10 and 5.10.14): MSIL triples map long double to
## double, so the IR says 'double @sqrtl(double)', but where the native long
## double is x87 extended (x86_64 Linux, x86_64 windows-gnu) the native ABI
## passes another value. msil-ld reports a live call that native lookup binds
## to a name of its long double list (sqrtl in libm.so.6, strtold in
## libc.so.6) after LTO, with '>>> referenced by' lines, and never binds it.
## The list also names nexttoward and nexttowardf (a long double parameter)
## and wcstold, and a reference that only takes the address of a listed
## function (expl kept in a global) is reported too, naming the global. A
## name in which 'f64x' or 'f128' is followed by the end of the name or by
## '_' is a native long double function as well (the section 12 row of
## 2026-10-23: glibc's _Float64x and _Float128 functions sqrtf64x,
## lgammaf64x_r, strtof64x_l, the narrowing f32addf64x, sqrtf128), whatever
## the IR signature says (double here), on x86_64 and aarch64 Linux alike
## (an EM_AARCH64 shared object for the aarch64 triple); sqrtf64 and
## sqrtf32x (_Float64 and _Float32x are double) bind as usual.
## On windows-msvc long double is double, and the same call binds; an
## explicit msil-import-module import is exempt (5.10.7: unchecked).

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: yaml2obj agg.yaml -o agg.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libagg.so.1 agg.o -o libagg.so.1
# RUN: llvm-as main.ll -o main.o

# DEFINE: %{err} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"

