# CHECK-DAG: {{^}}msil-ld: error: native function 'take_i128' (libagg.so.1) takes or returns a value that a P/Invoke cannot pass natively yet (phase 3){{$}}
# CHECK-DAG: {{^}}msil-ld: error: native function 'take_byval' (libagg.so.1) takes or returns a value that a P/Invoke cannot pass natively yet (phase 3){{$}}
# CHECK-DAG: {{^}}msil-ld: error: native function 'make_sret' (libagg.so.1) takes or returns a value that a P/Invoke cannot pass natively yet (phase 3){{$}}
# CHECK-DAG: {{^}}msil-ld: error: native function 'ret_vec' (libagg.so.1) takes or returns a value that a P/Invoke cannot pass natively yet (phase 3){{$}}
# CHECK-DAG: {{^}}msil-ld: error: native function 'ret_half' (libagg.so.1) takes or returns a value that a P/Invoke cannot pass natively yet (phase 3){{$}}
# CHECK-DAG: {{^}}msil-ld: error: native function 'addr_i128' (libagg.so.1) takes or returns a value that a P/Invoke cannot pass natively yet (phase 3){{$}}

## Once per function, although ret_pair has two calls.
# ONCE-COUNT-1: 'ret_pair' (libagg.so.1)
# ONCE-NOT:     'ret_pair' (libagg.so.1)
## Exactly seven errors: the seven above, and none for plain.
# SEVEN-COUNT-7: {{^}}msil-ld: error: {{.+}}
## The implicit patterns nowhere in the file: for a prefix made only of -DAG
## lines, --implicit-check-not checks only the text before the first match,
## and a COUNT line does not check them between its matches.
# ERR-NONE-NOT:   PLEASE submit
# ERR-NONE-NOT:   Stack dump
# ERR-NONE-NOT:   LLVM ERROR
# PLAIN-NONE-NOT: 'plain'

